<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sinan Pasha (Ottoman admiral)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1554">1554</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sinan Pasha was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapudan-pasha">Kapudan Pasha</a>, grand admiral of the Ottoman fleet, from about 1550 to 1554 and a brother of the grand <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> Rüstem Pasha. In August 1551, together with the corsair <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turgut-reis">Turgut Reis</a>, he besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli">Tripoli</a> and forced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> to surrender it, bringing Tripolitania under Ottoman rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sinan-pasha-ottoman-admiral.jpg" alt="Sinan Pasha (Ottoman admiral)" width="320" height="310" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yahia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tomb_of_Ottoman_Admiral_Sinan_Pasha_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
